DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-art-of-changing-habits\n\
 nHave you ever started a new routine with real determination\, only to sli
 de back into old patterns a few weeks later? Whether you want to change yo
 ur diet\, limit screen time\, or build a different daily rhythm\, shifting
  deeply ingrained habits takes more than willpower.\n\nJoin us for an inte
 ractive online class where you will explore practical\, compassionate stra
 tegies for making change that lasts. You will learn how to identify your o
 wn motivations and the rewards that keep current habits in place\, so you 
 can work with your habits instead of against them. You will also practice 
 approaching obstacles with curiosity rather than guilt\, which helps susta
 in momentum without the discouraging effects of self-judgment.\n\nTogether
 \, we will discuss how to link new behaviors to existing routines and cues
  in your life\, making them easier to remember and repeat. You will also l
 earn how to break big goals into small\, manageable steps that fit into a 
 busy day.\n\nYou will leave with a set of simple tools to begin shifting t
 he routines that matter most to you and a personal plan to work towards on
 e small change you are ready to make.\n\nThis class will not be recorded. 
 \n\nAttendance requirement for incentive points - at least 80% of the live
  session.  \n\nRequest disability accommodations and access info.\n\n\n\nC
 lass details are subject to change.
